      "confidence": 0.8,
      "curator_note": "Eq 8.5, lower scheme, alpha-i channel (arrow labelled 'ai'). n-butyl vinyl ether molecular ion (C6H12O, isomeric with hexanal). McLafferty-type gamma-H transfer to the terminal vinyl carbon followed by C-O cleavage; the C4H8 alkene retains the charge (IE(butene)=9.6 eV < IE(acetaldehyde)=10.2 eV printed -> butene dominates, 55%). Book draws 4 fishhook arcs (terminal-C gamma-H abstraction; ring C=C formation; C-O cleavage). Moves 1-3 (H transfer) are drawn; move 4 encodes the charge-retaining alkene ('i' inductive/heterolytic 2-electron C-O cleavage, the O-C4 pair collapsing to an O lone pair to give neutral acetaldehyde) and is not a separately drawn arc. Precursor written as the distonic oxa-allyl resonance form .CH2-CH=O(+)- (odd electron on the terminal carbon, as the page draws it; positive charge on O); butene localized as its distonic + on C4 / odd-e on C5 form. m/z curator-computed; 55% printed. [RECHECK 2026-07-24: arc count corrected 3->4 per a zoomed re-read; the gamma-H abstraction is drawn as TWO barbs (O-radical->H and the gamma C-H bond electron->O-H), not one.]"
    },
