      "curator_note": "Cross-link: M\u00d8D rule IMS_8_5_2 (src/data_generation/rules/IMS_chap8_examples.py). Its skeleton matches this scheme (gamma-H transfer, C-O cleavage, C=C alkene + C=O carbonyl, charge on the C4H8 butene) BUT the rule is MIS-ENCODED: the ether oxygen is over-valent (valence 4, two spurious H) and the adjacent carbon is over-valent (valence 5), giving reactant C6H15O rather than butyl vinyl ether C6H12O; its two product fragments total +2 / 2 radicals versus the +1/1 reactant, violating charge and spin conservation (guardrail-dropped). Not RDKit-substructure-testable (over-valent, not a valid molecule)."
